<p>This Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) describes how personal data of the users of {{ site_name }} (the “Site”) is processed and protected in accordance with the Law of the Republic of Belarus No. 99-Z of 7 May 2021 “On Personal Data Protection”. The Russian version of this document prevails.</p>

<h2>1. Data we process</h2>
<ul>
    <li>name, email address and phone number — when you book a trip, register or request a call back;</li>
    <li>booking details: dates, route, number of participants, wishes;</li>
    <li>reviews you leave after a trip (author name, rating and text);</li>
    <li>technical data: IP address and essential cookies required to sign in and to protect forms.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Purposes</h2>
<ul>
    <li>to process and confirm bookings and to contact you about your trip;</li>
    <li>to provide registration and the personal account;</li>
    <li>to send service emails: email confirmation, booking confirmation and status updates, password recovery;</li>
    <li>to publish reviews (only after moderation);</li>
    <li>to protect the Site against abuse (request rate limiting).</li>
</ul>
<p>Marketing emails are sent only with your separate consent, which you can withdraw in your profile settings.</p>

<h2>3. Cookies</h2>
<p>The Site uses essential cookies only: the sign-in session, the “Remember me” feature and protection of forms against request forgery. We do not use third-party advertising or analytics cookies.</p>

<h2>4. Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not sell or share your data with third parties. Data is stored on servers of our hosting provider and emails are delivered through an email service; these companies process data only on our behalf. The route map is loaded from OpenStreetMap servers, which receive your IP address.</p>

<h2>5. Retention</h2>
<p>Account data is kept until the account is deleted. You can delete your account yourself in the “Settings” section of your personal account. Booking records are kept for as long as needed to provide the service and comply with the law, and are deleted afterwards.</p>

<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
<ul>
    <li>to know which data about you is processed;</li>
    <li>to change your data in the personal account or on request;</li>
    <li>to withdraw consent and request deletion of your data;</li>
    <li>to file a complaint with the National Personal Data Protection Center of Belarus.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>Data is transmitted over an encrypted connection (HTTPS), passwords are stored only as cryptographic hashes, access is limited to authorized persons and software is updated regularly.</p>

<h2>8. Contact</h2>
<p>For any questions about personal data: <a href="tel:{{ settings.phoneLink }}">{{ settings.phone }}</a>, <a href="mailto:{{ settings.email }}">{{ settings.email }}</a>.</p>

<h2>9. Changes</h2>
<p>We may update this Policy; the current version is always published on this page together with the date of the last change.</p>
